had not returned after 5000 ms (parsed index 3, comparison violated). The boundary therefore reproduces from the follower's own appendEntries-driven commit staging, not only from a feeding leader.\n====================================================================================================\nf7da39e9771e40d29f8d7ec3d1c7d886-question-0 375638dfadfb453ca839444e302c3d7e-interpretation-0\nEXEC {\"d436029b08c5425aa5aec577901cb8ba\": [1, 3], \"0726bba116ac415fa38b99b96a88290f\": [1, 3], \"4185f1615cf54e4fbd4801044480416d\": [1, 3]}\nRATIONALE len 3495\nConclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. A leadership transfer that explicitly names a member the configuration marks as a non-voter is admitted, completes its future without error, and does not install that member as leader; the attempt instead forces an election round in which every member's term advances, leadership lands on a member the caller did not name, and leadership is absent for a measurable interval. Evidence, two receipts of the same experiment lineage. Parsed index 1 of receipt d436029b08c5425aa5aec577901cb8ba and of successor receipt 0726bba116ac415fa38b99b96a882\n...\nget and all other members at 4, one step beyond the rejected round) and its leaderless interval match exactly that path, while the control's single-step advance to 3 matches a successful transfer. Consequence under the exercised conditions: a caller that names a serving but non-voting member receives a completed transfer with no error, no transfer of authority, an extra election round that raises every member's term, and a leaderless interval whose length follows the configured election timeout.\n====================================================================================================\n830b0f3ff5a14266b056ad4a6d0c877b-question-0 d8355b1ced1e4de692e282fe742a1388-interpretation-0\nEXEC {\"cabc782e68fb4c98a4f82a9d4e62e07b\": [1, 3], \"14a6432138534293b361a796cd32bda8\": [1, 3], \"b89fc1d89b434e8c84a2219073e9a01c\": [1, 3]}\nRATIONALE len 3331\nConclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. A heartbeat executed on a goroutine other than the main RPC loop, as the fast-path contract permits, races the node's term update: when the stable-store write it performs takes long enough, the term it decided to persist can land after a higher term already persisted by the main thread, leaving the node below a term it had adopted. Once the term is below the current leader's term, the node stops rejecting an older leader's messages and replaces an entry it had already applied at the higher term with that leader's entry. Evidence. Consequ\n...\ng and FSM describing different histories. A clean-copy repeat of the same fixed experiment, receipt b89fc1d89b434e8c84a2219073e9a01c, reproduced the pair: parsed index 1 shows inversion_count=0 for the 200 no-delay attempts and parsed index 3 shows inversion_count=97 for the 200 jittered attempts, against 0 and 90 in the first run. The two runs therefore agree that the inversion is absent or rare without added store latency and common with 0-2 ms of it, while the exact count varies between runs.\n====================================================================================================\n533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-question-0 860f6951c3674a2fb52d3a867aa6f2bd-interpretation-0\nEXEC {\"7a54f3754b0b423aaf1ba6c0365367c0\": [1, 3], \"e49121154f514e39b6c1a37a2c353a4a\": [1, 2, 4, 5], \"13b7844febba4a6d80c7331818c943f6\": [1, 2, 4, 5]}\nRATIONALE len 3248\nConclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. VerifyLeader reports success although the leader can reach fewer voters than the voter quorum it sized, because acknowledgements arriving on non-voter replication streams are counted as support. Evidence from receipt 7a54f3754b0b423aaf1ba6c0365367c0 (completed, tests_passed, exit 0). Parsed index 1, the trigger: five members were bootstrapped, two were demoted to non-voters, and the leader's transport was disconnected in both